{
  "$description": "Scenes for the glass probe (tools/glass-probe/). Each is a stimulus we control, drawn pixel-exact, with Liquid Glass shapes over it. Units are points; shape offsets (x, y) are from the window's centre; colours are sRGB; r is the corner radius, absent for a capsule. Stimuli: flat {color}; edge {top, bottom}, split at the centre line; sine {low, high, period, axis}, a grating that varies along axis x or y, shifted by phase/phases of a period; tiles {levels, tile, color}, a centred grid of grey tiles (sRGB levels, row-major) with the first shape placed on every tile and color filling the margins. Shape sizes are Duo's: 48 button [KIT], 56 × 150 rail group [KIT], 76 × 220 and 220 × 96 capsules, a 360 × 180 panel with the sheet's 40 pt radius [KIT]. The sizes layout (it fits either Duo display) asks what makes large glass frost more: shapes of equal area and different short sides (360 × 56, 150 × 150), of equal short side and different areas (96 × 96, 420 × 96), 48 and 76 pt circles, and a large clear panel. Sets: what `npm run probe` captures, each at a position of Settings > Liquid Glass's clear-to-tinted slider (\"default\" removes it, as on a device nobody has changed); scene lists accept * wildcards.",
